      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;day-1---week-3&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Day 1 - Week 3 &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#day-1---week-3&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;topics-of-the-day&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Topics of the day &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#topics-of-the-day&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Simple Past Rules and Uses&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Verbs in Simple Past&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Regular verbs pronunciation&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Learning Objectives: &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;By the end of this lesson, you will be able to:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Describe past actions or interactions by using affirmative and negative sentences in the simple past.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Use common simple past verbs to explain completed actions during customer service calls (Example: processed requests, handled complaints, updated accounts).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Accurately pronounce regular past tense verb endings (-ed) to ensure clear and professional communication over the phone.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Introduction: &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today, you will learn how to talk about past situations in a call center. You will practice how to form sentences to describe what happened during a call, including things you did and things you didn’t do.&#xA;You will also learn common action words in their past form to explain tasks like helping customers, solving problems, and updating information.&#xA;Finally, you will practice how to pronounce regular verb endings correctly, so your speech is clear and professional when speaking with customers.&#xA;Important terms (Vocabulary):&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
